  "source": {
    "generator": null,
    "notes": "Horizon revaluation (nested VaR/CVA structure) via the CONDITIONAL nested-submodel statistic `nested_stat`. The outer model simulates a risk factor to a horizon H; for each outer scenario the inner submodel `innerBS` is re-run with its start price bound to that scenario's horizon price S_H, and the mean inner discounted payoff is the portfolio value in that scenario. The distribution of port_value across outer paths is the horizon P&L distribution from which VaR/expected-shortfall are read. Validated: the nested MC reproduces the closed-form Black-Scholes conditional value bs_ref per path; the marginal submodel_stat (marginal_bs) is a single constant BS(100), showing the conditional-vs-marginal distinction. See NESTED_STAT_EXAMPLE.md / NESTED_STAT_SCOPE.md."
  },
